      "id": "AUD-037-FUN001",
      "category": "FUN",
      "kind": "finding",
      "severity": "low",
      "status": "fixed",
      "title": "An expired request receives a new HTTP response budget",
      "releaseBlocking": true,
      "affectedFiles": [
        "src/bin/mhfe/serve.rs"
      ],
      "reproduction": "Call the real answer function on an accepted loopback socket with Duration::ZERO; the new regression was observed failing before the fix.",
      "expected": "A request-read timeout terminates the connection without further I/O or a fresh response budget.",
      "observed": "The baseline converted every read error into HTTP 400 and returned Ok after writing it; Windows separately failed the existing peer-closure limit.",
      "impact": "An expired public localhost request can enter a second response phase, unlike the standalone Python launcher. Connections remain capped; no secret or remote binding is introduced.",
      "recommendedFix": "Return TimedOut or WouldBlock immediately while retaining HTTP 400 for malformed input.",
      "implementedFix": "The match guard preserves the original timeout error; RAII closes both owned socket handles and the serving loop releases its active slot. Tests retain existing timing limits and malformed-input behavior.",
      "requiredVerification": "Deterministic baseline/patched socket control, kernel-read timeout and malformed-response controls, adjacent Rust/Python tests and complete new native CI.",
      "evidence": {
        "localOnly": true,
        "log": "commands/serve-expired-request-before.log",
        "sha256": "e3e30a63cb430e1f0e3c295d5835bd1608d18d7ed51c3ab88fc21775b4eeac95"
      }
